# =====================================================================
# This repo is a TEMPLATE. Only files generic to *any* video are tracked.
# Everything belonging to one particular episode -- footage, generated
# clips, scenes, compositions, editorial plans, renders -- is ignored and
# lives on disk only. A fresh checkout should be a working harness with no
# content.
#
# Two rules do the work, and the second exists because the first kept
# leaking:
#   1. Per-video FILES are ignored by path, grouped below with the reason.
#   2. Binary MEDIA is ignored by extension, everywhere, unconditionally.
# Rule 2 is the backstop: a new asset directory, a stray render written to
# the repo root, or a clip dropped somewhere nobody thought of is caught
# without anyone having to remember to add a path. Git history for binaries
# is permanent and cannot be undone without rewriting history, so the
# default has to be "no".
# =====================================================================

# --- Editor / OS / toolchain cruft ---
.DS_Store
*.log
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.env
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Binary media, anywhere in the tree (rule 2 above) ---
# Nothing tracked is one of these, and nothing tracked should become one:
# the engines are text, the content is not. Subtitles are here too -- an
# .srt is generated from a take by whisper, so it belongs to the episode
# exactly as much as the take does.
# Documentation images are the one carve-out, negated just below. Anything
# else you genuinely need committed is a deliberate act: `git add -f <path>`.
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.mov
*.webm
*.avi
*.gif
*.wav
*.mp3
*.flac
*.m4a
*.aac
*.ogg
*.srt
*.vtt
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp

# ...except documentation images, which ARE part of the template: a README
# screenshot or a diagram in docs/ explains the harness rather than belonging
# to one episode. Narrow on purpose -- docs/ only, so a stray render or a
# screencast still frame elsewhere is caught. Keep these small; they are as
# permanent as any other committed binary.
!docs/*.png
!docs/*.jpg
!docs/*.jpeg
!docs/*.webp

# --- Media: every asset directory holds one video's footage or output ---
raw/*
!raw/initial/
raw/initial/*
!raw/initial/.gitkeep
processed/*
screencasts/*
audio/*
memes/*
manim/*
remotion/*
reels/*
shorts/*
images/*
thumb/*
# video_clips/ holds short clips dropped in by hand for a plan to draw on.
# It was once the single tracked asset dir, on the theory that a small clip
# should travel with the repo; it is ignored now like every other, because
# "small" is not enforceable and a committed binary is forever.
video_clips/*
!*/.gitkeep

# --- Finished renders at the repo root (final.mp4 / .mkv / .srt) ---
/final.*

# --- Per-video Manim scenes ---
# `design.py` is the shared library: DESIGN.md's palette and roles, DesignScene,
# layout regions, spacing scale, audit_layout. Every other scene file is
# one episode's diagrams and snippets -- write fresh ones per video.
.manim/scenes/*
!.manim/scenes/.gitkeep
!.manim/scenes/design.py

# --- Per-video Remotion compositions ---
# The same split as .manim/scenes/, for the same reason. `remotion-clip`
# writes one file per clip here and registers it in Root.tsx, so this
# directory fills up with an episode's title cards, charts and code shots.
# Only the two structural compositions are template: `Hook` (the opening,
# built by hook-build) and `ReelEndCard` (the vertical CTA for extract-reels).
# Reusable pieces belong in .remotion/src/components/, which IS tracked.
.remotion/src/compositions/*
!.remotion/src/compositions/Hook.tsx
!.remotion/src/compositions/ReelEndCard.tsx

# --- Per-video editorial plan ---
# Names this episode's actual clips, gifs, punch lines and emoji, so it is
# NOT template code. The reusable engine it imports (scripts/timeline_lib.py)
# IS committed. Start a new video by writing a fresh plan against that engine;
# see docs/remotion-video-guidelines.md.
scripts/build_timeline_manifest.py
# Same split for the hook: scripts/hook_lib.py is the tracked engine,
# this is one episode's opening 30 seconds. See .claude/skills/hook-plan/.
scripts/build_hook_manifest.py

# --- Per-video Remotion timeline data ---
# Generated from the real durations of ignored media (processed/, manim/,
# memes/, screencasts/) -- meaningless in a checkout without those files.
# Regenerate with scripts/build_timeline_manifest.py.
.remotion/src/timeline-data.json
# The hook's equivalent. `python3 scripts/hook_lib.py --stub` writes a
# placeholder of both when you need to work on the template with no
# episode content present.
.remotion/src/hook-data.json

# --- Per-video planning notes ---
# `progress.md` is this video's todo list / working log -- it belongs to the
# episode, not the template. Durable lessons get promoted into CLAUDE.md,
# docs/ or a skill instead of being left here.
/plan.md
/progress.md
plans/*
!plans/.gitkeep

# --- Tool render caches and outputs (regenerable) ---
.manim/media/
.remotion/out/
